  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar Joint Response 2023 (MYMJR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cyclone Mocha was a powerful and deadly tropical cyclone in the North Indian Ocean which affected 
Myanmar and parts of Bangladesh in May 2023. It was the 1st cyclonic storm of the 2023 North Indian Ocean 
cyclone season. Mocha originated from a low-pressure area that was first noted on the 8 May. Mocha rapidly 
strengthened, peaking at Category 5-equivalent intensity on 14 May with winds of 280 km/h (175 mph), tying 
with Cyclone Fani as the strongest storm on ever record in the north Indian Ocean. Mocha slightly weakened 
before making landfall, and its conditions quickly became unfavourable. Mocha rapidly weakened once inland 
and dissipated shortly thereafter.

Tearfund Myanman with local partners KBC &amp; CPM will provide integrated MPC and Shelter support to address the urgent needs of 1,155 most affected HHs (5,775 people) in Sittwe and Mrauk-U districts (Rakhine State).</narrative>
  </description>
